# MIRAL Soft enforcement configuration.
# Read by the git hooks in .git/hooks/ and by .github/workflows/ci.yml, which reads
# these same keys so the local and the server-side check can never disagree about
# what is covered (R-17). Install the hooks with the commands in CLAUDE.md; they live
# in a clone, so a fresh clone needs them again.

# Expected committer identity (R-03, R-19). This is a private game plugin, so the
# project identity is the owner's in-game name and a GitHub noreply address. No
# personal address is exposed in the repository. This must match what docs/project.md
# declares.
OWNER_NAME=Sanaka
OWNER_EMAIL=20637644+miralsoft@users.noreply.github.com

# Space-separated globs whose staged files are checked for em-dash characters (I-02).
#
# These are shell `case` patterns, where `*` also matches `/`. So `*.md` already covers
# every markdown file at any depth, and listing `docs/*.md` as well would add nothing.
#
# The scope is every file that carries prose a human reads, which since foundation
# 2.0.0 explicitly includes source comments: six em-dashes sat in XML doc comments in
# this repository for months because the globs stopped at markdown. It also includes
# the JSON catalogues, because the release notes and the language catalogues are the
# most user-facing prose the project ships.
CONTENT_GLOBS=*.md *.cs *.json *.ps1 *.yml

# Material the project did not write and must not rewrite, skipped rather than
# reported. Empty on purpose: this repository contains no delivered third-party text.
# The foundation clone lives at .foundation-docs/ and is excluded from git entirely,
# so it is never staged and needs no entry here.
CONTENT_EXCLUDE=
